    {
      "id": "rn_YXZBtqvvgTHppc4Q::L2::Q9",
      "moduleId": "rn_YXZBtqvvgTHppc4Q::L2",
      "stem": "Draw-verbalise the box diagram for four electrons in a 2p sub-shell, naming the rule each step obeys.",
      "misconceptionClass": "box diagram application",
      "kind": "application",
      "modelAnswer": "First three: single arrows up in px, py, pz (Hund's rule). Fourth: pairs into px with a down-arrow, opposite spin (Pauli exclusion principle), leaving py and pz singly occupied.",
